    <string name="about_termuide">About TermuIDE</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %1$s · %2$s</string>
    <string name="about_fork">TermuIDE is an independent fork of TermuC by RainbowC0 and contributors, maintained by AM-RTS and contributors. It is not an official TermuC or Termux release.</string>
    <string name="about_differences">This fork adds a Material 3 Compose interface, the Sora editor, durable unsaved-document recovery, optional auto-save, shared run configurations, basic Python and Java execution, and save/debugger hardening. C/C++ tooling continues to use Termux, clangd and GDB. Projects use termuide.json; legacy termuc.json is not detected automatically.</string>
    <string name="about_license">Free software under the GNU General Public License version 3. You may copy, modify and redistribute it under that license. Provided without warranty, including merchantability or fitness for a particular purpose. Copyright remains with the respective authors; see acknowledgements and file notices.</string>
    <string name="about_credits">Thanks to RainbowC0 and TermuC contributors; MrIkso and CodeEditor contributors; Tah Wei Hoon and TextWarrior contributors (Apache 2.0); Rosemoe and Sora contributors (LGPL 2.1 or later); AndroidX, Material and Kotlin contributors (Apache 2.0); and the Termux community. External runtimes are installed separately and retain their own licenses.</string>
